Subject: [PATCH 3/3] aiter: route the M=64 decode down_proj to flydsl splitK=4

REJECTED -- DO NOT APPLY. No measurable end-to-end effect. Kept as a recorded negative
result, and as the counterexample that closes the in-situ-benchmarking thread; see
FINDINGS.md #7.

WHY THIS ONE LOOKED DIFFERENT
  Patch 0001 came from an isolated graph race and regressed the server. This row came from
  a whole-decoder-layer race (analysis/bench_decode_layer.py: qkv -> paged attention ->
  o_proj -> gate_up -> silu_and_mul -> down_proj, captured in one graph), which had already
  been validated by reproducing 0001's regression from kernels alone. It was the only
  configuration out of ~54 candidates across all four decode shapes that beat the shipping
  one in situ by more than the harness's own control spread.

MEASUREMENT
  The same kernel, the same shape (M=64, N=4096, K=14336), measured three ways:
    aiter tuner, eager            flydsl:3522 30.05 us  vs hipblaslt:440151 28.96 us -> hipblaslt
    isolated graph, 1120 MB ws    flydsl:3522 29.245 us vs torch            28.991 us -> torch
    in situ, whole decoder layer  +0.54% of the layer step, bias-corrected  -> flydsl
  Three methods, three different winners.

  End-to-end, 6 paired restart-to-restart rounds, arm order flipped every round
  (DEPLOY=analysis/deploy_down_flydsl.py PREFIX=abd analysis/ab_campaign.sh),
  bench/ against a bench/ baseline:
    base 2640.788 tok/s   cand 2639.495 tok/s   -0.049% +/- 0.088% (2*SEM)
    per-round deltas: -0.064 -0.252 -0.042 +0.025 +0.043 -0.003 %   (2 up, 4 down)
    base range [2639.390, 2643.154]  cand range [2636.492, 2640.656]  -- OVERLAPPING
    mean TPOT 20.3548 -> 20.3639 ms (+0.045%)
  Restart-to-restart spread of the base arm alone is 0.142% over the same 6 restarts, so
  the measured delta is a third of the noise floor it would have to clear. Nothing here.

  Engagement was verified, so this is a null result about a live change and not about a
  change that never loaded: with the row present the server logs 0 "not found tuned config"
  lines for M:64, N:4096, K:14336 (1 without it), and the merged table
  /tmp/aiter_configs/bf16_tuned_gemm.csv carries the row.

ACCURACY
  gsm8k 5-shot, run against the live server with the row applied
  (eval_results/down_flydsl3522_20260820_124050):
    strict-match   0.8461 +/- 0.0099   vs 0.8415 baseline   (gate >= 0.8213)
    flexible       0.8476 +/- 0.0099   vs 0.8431 baseline
  PASSES. Within one stderr of baseline, and slightly above it. Accuracy is not why this
  is rejected.

APPLY
  cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && patch -p1 < <this file>
  rm -rf /tmp/aiter_configs      # merged table is regenerated only when absent
  # then restart the server: the GEMM table is consumed at HIP-graph capture time
  # revert: python3 analysis/deploy_down_flydsl.py revert

BASE
  aiter d9e5ef7ce08ee7045d583aed768cff41aa9210fe. This patch only CREATES a file --
  aiter/configs/model_configs/llama31_8b_bf16_tuned_gemm.csv does not exist in the shipped
  tree, so the pristine base is its absence and `revert` is a delete. Confirmed free of a
  duplicate key before deploying:
    cd /sgl-workspace/aiter/aiter/configs
    grep -l ",64,4096,14336," bf16_tuned_gemm.csv model_configs/*bf16_tuned_gemm*.csv   # no match
  Unlike 0001, this touches no other model's configuration.

RELATION TO THE OTHER PATCHES
  Independent of 0001 and 0002 and measured on its own. 0001 also carried a row for this
  shape (hipblaslt:440151); the two are mutually exclusive and 0001 is rejected anyway.

